{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"GHSA-997q-gvvc-jwmx","published":"2026-10-22T16:43:59Z","modified":"2026-10-22T17:00:05.173770092Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-114121"],"summary":"Electron: openExternal permission requests can be attributed to the wrong origin","details":"### Impact\nRequests to open external protocol URLs could be attributed to a document other than the one that asked for them, so the `requestingUrl` passed to `session.setPermissionRequestHandler` was a trusted origin for a launch untrusted content had requested. An origin-based handler could therefore let untrusted content launch an OS-registered external application.\n\nApps are only affected if they grant `openExternal` based on the requesting origin and let untrusted content open or navigate windows. Apps whose permission handler denies `openExternal` for untrusted content are not affected.\n\n### Workarounds\nDeny the `openExternal` permission for untrusted content, or deny the windows it opens with `setWindowOpenHandler`.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n* `45.0.0-alpha.5`\n* `44.3.0`\n* `43.7.0`\n* `42.11.3`\n\n### For more information\nIf you have any questions or comments about this advisory, email us at [security@electronjs.org](mailto:security@electronjs.org)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"electron","ecosystem":"npm","purl":"pkg:npm/electron"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"42.11.3"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/10/GHSA-997q-gvvc-jwmx/GHSA-997q-gvvc-jwmx.json"}},{"package":{"name":"electron","ecosystem":"npm","purl":"pkg:npm/electron"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"43.0.0-alpha.1"},{"fixed":"43.7.0"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/advisories/github-reviewed/2026/10/GHSA-997q-gvvc-jwmx/GHSA-997q-gvvc-jwmx.json"}},{"package":{"name":"electron","ecosystem":"npm","purl":"pkg:npm/electron"},"ranges":[{"typ